# Normalise to LF in the repository, and check out LF everywhere.
#
# The privacy notice is compared byte-for-byte against its generated
# TypeScript copy (tests/privacy/logs-audit.test.ts). With core.autocrlf=true
# on Windows the markdown is rewritten to CRLF on checkout while the generated
# module keeps LF, so the test fails on a clean tree for a reason that has
# nothing to do with the content. Pinning LF makes the comparison meaningful
# and platform-independent.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets must never be converted.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.ico binary
